.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-DELETE-ACCESS-KEY 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-delete-access-key \- delete one of the logged-in user's own access keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam delete-access-key
.BR \-\-accessKeyId | \-k
.I ACCESSKEYID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes the access key identified by \fIACCESSKEYID\fR via the eam service's
.I delete-access-key
action. Only the logged-in user's own access keys may be deleted this way.
.PP
Self-service: any authenticated user may delete their own access keys, no
administrator privileges required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-accessKeyId " " \fIACCESSKEYID\fR
ID of the access key to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The access key was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is not
authenticated, or no access key with that ID exists for the caller. If the
failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored
credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam delete-access-key --accessKeyId AKIAEXAMPLE
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-access-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-access-keys (1)
